== test/fixtures/Makefile.state-recipe-context
   1 0 0  0  0 \t | # Which lines keep or end the recipe context (`make help` relies on it: a tab-indented
   2 0 0  0  0 \t | # ## line is a recipe line inside a rule, and a doc outside one). Each block is
   3 0 0  0  0 \t | #   a context: a documented rule with a recipe (inside a rule) or an assignment (outside)
   4 0 0  0  0 \t | #   the line under test
   5 0 0  0  0 \t | #   a tab-indented doc
   6 0 0  0  0 \t | #   a target, next-N: documented only if the line under test leaves the parser outside
   7 0 0  0  0 \t | #   a rule (as in GNU Make)
   8 0 0  0  0 \t | # Only the lines where makefile-doc.awk agrees with GNU Make are here (the others are in
   9 0 0  0  0 \t | # the fixtures of known bugs).
